% A collection must not reclaim the file a vector device is writing.
% Run through the pdfwrite device by run-vecout-gc-test.sh.
%
% The paginated single-file writer keeps its across-page bookkeeping --
% including the open output file -- in a dictionary in global memory, so
% that the save and restore a job wraps around each page cannot rewind
% it. A file object lives in local memory whatever dictionary holds it,
% and a global dictionary is not a root for local memory (PLRM 3.7.2),
% so a collection between two pieces of output must still find that file
% reachable. If it does not, the entity is reclaimed, its slot is reused
% by whatever is allocated next, and the device writes through whatever
% now sits there.

newpath 10 10 moveto 100 10 lineto 100 100 lineto closepath fill

1 vmreclaim

% enough short-lived allocation to reuse the slots the collection freed
/junk [ 0 1 4000 { pop 40 string } for ] def
/junk null def

1 vmreclaim

newpath 20 20 moveto 120 20 lineto 120 120 lineto closepath fill
showpage

% a second page, so the file is written across a page boundary as well
newpath 30 30 moveto 130 30 lineto 130 130 lineto closepath fill
1 vmreclaim
showpage
